### Slide 14: Precision Engineering: Threshold Tuning & Zero-Alarm Operations
* **Target Time:** `16:00 - 17:15` (1 minute 15 seconds)
* **Visual:** `assets/v2_confusion_matrices.png` (Confusion Matrix showing 838 TN, 82 TP, 4 FP, 0 FN); Dual-threshold operating policy explanation.
* **Delivery Cues:** Point directly to the confusion matrix cell showing "0 False Negatives". Explain the business rationale behind the dual-threshold policy.

```text
[CLICK SLIDE 14]
[POINT TO CONFUSION MATRIX]

In enterprise cybersecurity operations, high detection recall means nothing if it comes at the expense of false alarms. If an AI system blocks paying customers, the Chief Revenue Officer will order it turned off by Tuesday morning.

Let us inspect our empirical confusion matrix on the left.
Across the 154-minute chaotic blind test:
First: Look at the False Negatives. It is exactly ZERO. Out of 82 attack windows, the model missed none.
Second: Out of 842 normal traffic windows, the model correctly allowed 838 windows, yielding an operational specificity of 99.5%. It produced only 4 borderline false positives under extreme volatility.

To translate these metrics into zero business disruption, we implemented a dual-threshold enforcement policy:

We establish two operational thresholds:
1. Hard Block Threshold at $\tau = 0.85$: When the probability exceeds 0.85, the gateway issues immediate HTTP 403 blocks.
2. Soft Challenge Threshold at $\tau = 0.50$: When the score sits in the ambiguous zone between 0.50 and 0.85, we do NOT block traffic. Instead, the gateway initiates "tarpitting"—artificially injecting a 200ms delay into responses—or issues a lightweight cryptographic Proof-of-Work challenge.

To an automated botnet running 10,000 parallel threads, a 200ms latency penalty multiplies their connection pool costs and destroys their stuffing throughput. 
To a human user logging into an application, a 200ms delay is completely unnoticeable. 

This dual-threshold strategy bridges the gap between machine learning probability and real-world business continuity.
```

